  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{x}=\\{1,2,3, \\ldots \\ldots . .20\\} \\\\ & \\mathrm{R}_1=\\{(\\mathrm{x}, \\mathrm{y}): 2 \\mathrm{x}-3 \\mathrm{y}=2\\} \\\\ & \\mathrm{R}_2=\\{(\\mathrm{x}, \\mathrm{y}):-5 \\mathrm{x}+4 \\mathrm{y}=0\\}\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{R}_1=\\{(4,2),(7,4),(10,6),(13,8),(16,10),(19,12)\\} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{R}_2=\\{(4,5),(8,10),(12,15),(16,20)\\}\n\\end{aligned}$\nin $R_1 6$ element needed\nin $R_2 4$ element needed\nSo, total $6+4=10$ element",
    "image": null
  },
